# 📘 FramePulse — Complete Project & Viva Guide for Group Members
*(Game Performance & Review Analytics System — CT-263 Object-Oriented Analysis & Design)*

Ye file group ke **har member** ke liye banayi gayi hai taake lab demonstration (**CCA**) aur written report (**CCP**) dono ke waqt har member ko 100% clear ho ke hamara project kya hai, kyun banaya gaya hai, diagrams ka kya matlab hai, aur Java code mein kaun sa OOP concept kahan laga hua hai.

---

## 1. 🎯 Project Idea (Asaan Alfaaz Mein)
Jab koi naya PC game release hota hai, to gamers aur developers ko do cheezon ka pata lagana hota hai:
1. **Hardware Performance (Telemetry):** Game alag-alag resolutions (`1080p`, `1440p`, `4K`) par kitne **FPS (Frames Per Second)** de raha hai, **CPU aur GPU** kitna % use kar raha hai, aur kya game **crash** ho raha hai ya nahi?
2. **Player Reviews & Ratings:** Gamers ko game ki story, gameplay aur optimization kaisi lagi (**1 se 5 stars** + written comment)?

**Masla (Problem):** Aam taur par FPS benchmarks alag tools mein hote hain aur reviews alag websites par, aur reviews mein aksar spam/toxic comments aa jate hain jinse game ki average rating kharab ho jati hai.

**Hamara Solution (`FramePulse`):**
Humne **Java Swing** mein ek desktop application banayi hai jahan:
- **Gamer** apna gameplay FPS session (`LOG-301`) aur game review (`REV-901`) submit karta hai.
- **Admin** toxic ya spam reviews ko reject/delete karta hai aur sahi reviews ko approve karta hai.
- **Analytics Engine** automatically har game ki **Average Rating**, **Average FPS**, aur **System Stability Score (out of 100)** calculate karta hai, graph banata hai, aur **Game Report (`REP-001`)** generate karta hai.

---

## 2. 📝 Report Sections (CCP Written Report ke Liye Ready Content)

### A. Introduction
Modern video games require continuous monitoring of both technical performance (frame rates, hardware utilization, crash frequency) and player satisfaction. **FramePulse (Game Performance & Review Analytics System)** is an Object-Oriented Java application that integrates hardware telemetry logging with moderated community reviews to produce real-time stability metrics and analytical reports.

### B. Objectives
1. To design and implement a modular Java desktop application following core **OOAD principles** (Abstraction, Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, Composition, and Design Patterns).
2. To enable gamers to log hardware telemetry (**FPS, CPU %, GPU %, resolution, crash status**) and submit star ratings with written reviews.
3. To provide administrators with moderation controls (**Approve, Reject, Delete**) to prevent spam/toxic reviews from distorting game ratings.
4. To compute automated analytics (**Average Rating, Average FPS, System Stability Score**) and generate exportable reports.

### C. Problem Statement
Existing platforms separate hardware benchmarking from user review platforms, forcing players and developers to consult multiple disconnected sources. Furthermore, unmoderated review systems are vulnerable to spam and review-bombing, while raw FPS numbers alone do not reflect crash stability. A unified system is needed to combine moderated player ratings with multi-session hardware telemetry into a single stability index.

---

## 3. 🧱 OOP Concepts & Design Patterns (Viva Mein Sabse Zyada Pucha Jane Wala Part)

Miss jab lab mein puchein ke **"Aapne OOP ke kaun-kaun se concepts aur Design Pattern kahan use kiye hain?"**, to ye table dikhana aur batana:

| OOP Concept / Pattern | Hamare Code Mein Kahan Hai? | Viva Mein Kaise Samjhayein? |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1. Abstraction** | `src/User.java` (`abstract class User`) aur `src/Refreshable.java` (`interface`) | "`User` ek abstract class hai kyunki system mein koi generic 'User' nahi hota — har user ya to `Gamer` hota hai ya `Admin`. Ismein `getRole()` abstract method hai." |
| **2. Inheritance (Generalization)** | `Gamer extends User` (`src/Gamer.java`), `Admin extends User` (`src/Admin.java`) | "`Gamer` aur `Admin` dono `User` class se `userId`, `username`, `email`, `login()`, aur `logout()` inherit karte hain taake code duplicate na ho." |
| **3. Polymorphism** | `getRole()` in `User.java`, `Gamer.java`, `Admin.java` + `@Override toString()` + `@Override paintComponent(Graphics g)` | "`getRole()` method `Gamer` ke liye `'Gamer'` aur `Admin` ke liye `'Admin'` return karta hai (Method Overriding / Runtime Polymorphism)." |
| **4. Encapsulation** | Saari model classes (`Game.java`, `Review.java`, `PerformanceLog.java`) | "Har class ke data fields `private` hain (jaise `-averageFps`, `-rating`, `-comment`) aur unhein sirf public getters/setters ke zariye access kiya jata hai." |
| **5. Composition (Strong Has-A)** | `Game.java` contains `List<PerformanceSession>` and `List<Review>` | "Class diagram mein `Game` ke saath filled diamond (`*--`) laga hai: `Review` aur `PerformanceLog` kisi `Game` ka hissa hain; agar `Game` delete ho to uske logs aur reviews bhi khatam ho jate hain." |
| **6. Association** | `Gamer` submits `Review` & generates `PerformanceLog`; `Admin` manages `Game` | "Ek `Gamer` multiple reviews (`0..*`) aur performance logs (`0..*`) submit kar sakta hai." |
| **7. Singleton Design Pattern** | `src/AnalyticsEngine.java` (`AnalyticsEngine.getInstance()`) | "Pure system mein calculations karne ke liye sirf ek hi `AnalyticsEngine` object chahiye hota hai, isliye humne `private` constructor aur `public static getInstance()` ke saath **Singleton Pattern** lagaya hai." |

